    {
      "id": "semantic-zoom-architecture-instructions",
      "type": "content",
      "label": "Four Mechanisms, Side by Side",
      "root": false,
      "position": {
        "x": -2060,
        "y": 260
      },
      "width": 760,
      "height": 300,
      "ports": [
        {
          "id": "root",
          "label": "root",
          "direction": "bidirectional",
          "dataType": "any",
          "angle": 210
        },
        {
          "id": "guided-by",
          "key": "guided-by",
          "label": "guided by",
          "direction": "bidirectional",
          "dataType": "any",
          "angle": 180,
          "role": "relationship",
          "allowedEdgeTypes": [
            "reference"
          ],
          "metadata": {
            "relationship": true,
            "role": "relationship"
          }
        }
      ],
      "visible": true,
      "showLabel": true,
      "data": {
        "identity": {
          "graphId": "semantic-zoom-architecture"
        },
        "content": {
          "kind": "markdown",
          "value": "# Four mechanisms, side by side\n\nWhat exists today, read from the four files directly.\n\n| Mechanism | File | Reads | Does | Never does |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| Content scale | nodeContentScale.js | camera zoom | scales a node's rendered content to match its frame | move a position |\n| Per-node level | (data._semanticLevel) | an authored or assigned string | picks which of a node's own views to show | affect any other node |\n| Workspace bands | graphViewPresentation.js, graphWorkspace.js | screen occupancy percent | swaps a whole unfocused graph to glyph/icon/summary/detail/expanded | apply to a focused graph |\n| View sequence | viewSequence.js | a 0-3 resolution number | picks a named view by fallback order or by threshold | reflow anything |\n\n## Where they already touch\n\n`occupancyResolution()` in viewResolution.js converts an occupancy percent into the 0-3 resolution scale, so two of the four already share a translation. The other two (content scale's raw zoom, and the per-node level string) do not participate in that conversion at all.\n\n## What a unified model would need to answer\n\n1. One number (or one small, named set of numbers) every mechanism reads, replacing occupancy percent, 0-3 resolution, and the level string.\n\n2. Whether any level of that model is allowed to repack node.position, and if so, only ever as a view-time transform, never a write to the saved graph.\n\n3. Where the band boundaries live once there is one table: probably one place, the way WHEEL_CONTRACT is one ordered list wheel.js and every wheel handler reads.\n\n## Not in scope\n\nRedesigning content scaling itself, or the semantic ring / browse-mode node loading system, which is a fifth, separate mechanism not covered here."
        },
        "interfaceContract": {
          "version": 1,
          "receivesViewContent": true
        }
      },
