          "portId": "affects"
        }
      ],
      "visible": true,
      "showLabel": false,
      "data": {
        "title": "What \"semantic zoom\" means depends on which file you are reading",
        "statement": "components/NodeGraph/nodeContentScale.js scales a node's rendered content with the camera and never touches its position. A node's data._semanticLevel picks which of its own views (detail/summary/icon) to render. components/GraphEditor/utils/graphWorkspace.js and graphViewPresentation.js collapse a whole unfocused graph in the workspace to glyph/icon/summary/detail/expanded by what percentage of the screen it occupies. components/GraphEditor/utils/viewSequence.js gives the fallback order between named views, on a resolution scale that overlaps the workspace bands' but is read differently. Each reads its own units (a zoom number, a level string, an occupancy percent, a 0-3 resolution) and none of the four consult each other.",
        "impact": "Every graph that is authored with comfortable, non-overlapping spacing (which is how graphs are built, node by node) looks sparse at any zoom short of the one where it collapses entirely. A person cannot tell, from the four mechanisms' names alone, which one governs what they are looking at, and neither could I until I read all four files side by side.",
        "urgency": "medium",
        "definitionKey": "idea-problem",
        "_classBinding": {
          "key": "idea-problem",
          "sourceRef": "github://mikemartinez1974/public/templates/idea-template/classes/nodes/idea-problem.node-class.node",
