            "relationship": true,
            "role": "relationship"
          }
        }
      ],
      "visible": true,
      "showLabel": false,
      "data": {
        "title": "Skip the unified model and the reflow question; author dense graphs tightly to begin with",
        "description": "Do not build a unified threshold model or a repack mechanism. Instead, author every dense graph, starting with this one, with a tight, considered layout, so there is nothing to repack.",
        "tradeoffs": "Cheap and immediate, with no architecture risk. But it does not scale: every future template, and every graph a person builds by hand, inherits the same tendency to spread out for editing comfort, and the four uncoordinated mechanisms stay uncoordinated — there is just less waste to see, not less confusion about which one governs what.",
        "definitionKey": "idea-alternative",
        "_classBinding": {
          "key": "idea-alternative",
          "sourceRef": "github://mikemartinez1974/public/templates/idea-template/classes/nodes/idea-alternative.node-class.node",
