      "visible": true,
      "showLabel": false,
      "data": {
        "title": "Can occupancy percent, 0-3 resolution, and _semanticLevel become one number?",
        "question": "The wheel contract worked because there was one kind of event to arbitrate. Here there are four different things being measured (screen occupancy, a graph's own resolution claims, a node's authored level, camera zoom). Do they really reduce to one number, or does unifying the vocabulary mean translation functions between three numbers, not one table?",
        "status": "answered",
        "answer": "Answered by Michael: one continuous scale from 0 to 3, the resolution scale viewResolution.js already defines, used for both focused and unfocused graphs alike. Resolution 3 (full, unfocused detail) will eventually sit behind a paywall, so the model needs to carry an entitlement cap alongside the occupancy-derived resolution, not only a display threshold. What exactly the cap covers is still open (see the new question).",
        "definitionKey": "idea-question",
        "_classBinding": {
          "key": "idea-question",
