      "data": {
        "title": "What does capping resolution at a lower ceiling for a free account actually look like?",
        "question": "Resolution 3 will eventually be paywalled, per Michael. Does that mean a free account can never reach full, unfocused detail on any graph past some resolution short of 3, or only that specific high-resolution views are gated? What does hitting the ceiling look like: nothing past it, a locked or blurred view, or a fixed upgrade prompt?",
        "status": "answered",
        "answer": "Answered by Michael: a hard stop, no tease. The camera simply stops before reaching the paywalled range for a free account; there is no blurred preview or upgrade prompt at the ceiling.",
